00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
The Burning Bed is a 1984 American television crime drama film directed by Robert Greenwald and
starring Farrah Fawcett, Paul Le Mat, Richard Masur, Grace Zabriskie, and James Callahan.

13
01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,285
Adapted by Rose Leiman Goldemberg from the 1980 non-fiction novel of the same name by Faith McNulty, it follows battered
housewife Francine Hughes and her trial for the murder of her abusive ex-husband, James Berlin "Mickey" Hughes.

14
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
Hughes set fire to the bed her husband was sleeping in at their Dansville, Michigan home on
March 9, 1977, after thirteen years of physical domestic abuse at his hands.

15
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
It aired on NBC on October 8, 1984.

16
01:16:11,428 --> 01:16:17,428
The film premiered with a household share of 36.2, ranking it the seventeenth  highest rated
movie to air on network television and NBC's highest rated television movie.

17
01:20:57,142 --> 01:21:03,142
The Burning Bed was met with critical acclaim, receiving eight
nominations at the 37th Primetime Emmy Awards.

18
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
It was also nominated for three Golden Globe Awards, with Le Mat winning the
award for Best Supporting Actor in a Miniseries or Television Film.

19
01:30:28,571 --> 01:30:34,571
The film explores themes of domestic violence, killer, biting, angry, detached.

20
01:35:14,285 --> 01:35:20,285
The tone is emotional.
